Coders extract \delta by applying the following rule to each candidate pair (\psi_i, \psi_j):

· If the text states or clearly implies that an increase in \psi_i leads to an increase in \psi_j, code +1.
· If an increase in \psi_i leads to a decrease in \psi_j, code -1.
· If the relationship is acknowledged but the direction is ambiguous or contested by characters, code 0 (the hypothesis is retained as non‑directional for later empirical resolution).

