Appendix J. Cross‑Cultural Measurement Invariance Protocol

J.1 Sequential Testing

Invariance of the AEGI is tested across Western individualist and MENA collectivist groups using multiple‑group CFA:

1. Configural invariance: Same factor structure, loadings and intercepts free across groups.
2. Metric invariance: Loadings constrained equal. \Delta CFI \ge -0.01 and \Delta RMSEA \le 0.015 relative to configural model indicate acceptable metric invariance.
3. Scalar invariance: Loadings and intercepts constrained equal. Same \Delta criteria applied relative to metric model.

If scalar invariance fails, we apply alignment optimization (Asparouhov & Muthén, 2014), which estimates group‑specific intercepts and loadings while minimizing non‑invariance, and then tests whether the latent means can be validly compared. This fallback is pre‑registered.

J.2 Interpretation

If scalar invariance holds (or alignment supports comparability), the group comparison of the Ritual × Group interaction is interpretable as a genuine cultural difference in the buffering mechanism. If invariance cannot be established, the interaction test is still conducted but the results are explicitly bounded by the measurement non‑equivalence caveat.

